ican-leaning northwest Georgia seat that has not been a regular battleground. John Cowan won a contested GOP primary in June and enters the fall with a large financial edge, having raised roughly $2.3 million to Chris Harden's $76,000, aided by outside spending on his side. Harden ended September with almost no cash on hand.\n\nA single September poll of likely voters showed Harden up two points, but prediction markets still put the Republican's chances around 95 percent, and the district's partisan lean points the other way. A favorable national environment for Democrats and the lack of an incumbent give the party a modest opening, but the fundamentals favor Cowan to hold the seat, with the main question being the size of the margin rather than the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1084, "margin": -8.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0742, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1332, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1182, "margin": -8.0}]}